Use the native CONFIG_SITE compiler commands for sidplay2's ABI flags.

The shared native CONFIG_SITE already supplies the compiler launcher, forced
ABI header and stdio overlay. Copying shell-quoted CMake flags into Autoconf's
CFLAGS/CXXFLAGS passes literal quotes to Clang, producing an empty include
filename. Keep the platform defines and linker flags without duplicating ABI
options in a different flag-string format.

Upstream: PS5-only; requires the native catalogue's shared CONFIG_SITE.

--- a/depends/common/sidplay2/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/depends/common/sidplay2/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -11,8 +11,8 @@
                                    autoreconf -vif builders/hardsid-builder &&
                                    autoreconf -vif libsidutils
                     CONFIGURE_COMMAND ${CMAKE_COMMAND} -E env
-                      "CFLAGS=${CMAKE_C_FLAGS}"
-                      "CXXFLAGS=${CMAKE_CXX_FLAGS} -DHAVE_UNIX"
+                      "CFLAGS=-DTARGET_POSIX -DTARGET_FREEBSD"
+                      "CXXFLAGS=-DTARGET_POSIX -DTARGET_FREEBSD -DHAVE_UNIX"
                       "LDFLAGS=${CMAKE_EXE_LINKER_FLAGS}"
                       <SOURCE_DIR>/configure
                       --prefix=${OUTPUT_DIR}
